<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Keppel, 3rd Earl of Albemarle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1724">1724</a>–<a href="/years/1772">1772</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Earl of Albemarle</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Keppel, 3rd Earl of Albemarle, was a British army officer and politician. A favourite of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernest-augustus-king-of-hanover">Duke of Cumberland</a>, he served at Fontenoy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-culloden">Culloden</a>. In 1762, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a>, he commanded the expedition that besieged and captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/havana">Havana</a>, and as its military governor he gained a great fortune from the prize money and levies on the city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-keppel-3rd-earl-of-albemarle.jpg" alt="George Keppel, 3rd Earl of Albemarle" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francis Cotes · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:George_Keppel,_3rd_Earl_of_Albemarle,_by_Francis_Cotes_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
